From 0a0ff8e373d74eaa767da738c4cdd4a686dde4b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:30:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Freeciv45 top strip and right-edge buttons: the empire's
 numbers and the overviews replace the sidebar

A new Qt client option, gui_qt_freeciv45_edges ("Freeciv45 top strip and
edge buttons", default on), hides the left sidebar and puts two frames
around the map instead:

- A top strip with research (the tech, bulbs per turn and the turns left),
  gold and income, the tax, luxury and science rates, culture with the
  history gained per turn, the year and turn, and End turn. Each number is a
  button: research opens the science report, gold the economy report, the
  rates the rates dialog, culture the nations report, the turn returns to
  the map. End turn is greyed out and stands out as the sidebar's Turn Done
  did.
- A right-edge column of round buttons: Map, Research, Nations, Cities,
  Units and Economy, which open today's reports, and More, a menu for
  demographics, wonders, top cities, achievements and the spaceship.

Switching the option off brings the sidebar back and removes both frames.
The strip refreshes with the sidebar's tooltips, which follow the player,
research and turn packets. Both frames are themed in the NightStalker and
System resource.qss. First slice of notes/freeciv45/ui/panels.md section 8;
the notification badges and the "what next" button come later.
